import GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcWord
import GQ2.Dyadic.SqCore.GradedClassFour

/-!
# W85-M6BUILD: the `M6` ansatz at class four, and the widened shape

Wave 84 (`GQ2/Dyadic/Instances/MpcWord.lean`) reduced `MpcPivShift 2` - the whole residue of the
`ℚ₂(√−10)` row - to one word identity, showed it is decided at a finite class, and proved classes
at most three free.  It left two things: the class-four rung, whose kill was a hand computation
in the Magnus model, and the widened shape, in which the `B̄` and `D̄` letters carry χ-legal `Ā`
and `C̄₀` factors.  This module lands both.

## What lands

1. **The class-four defect in closed form** (§1, §2).  For arbitrary `λ₂`-corrections the `M6`
   core word is, modulo `λ₄`, the marked relator times an explicit product of eight brackets
   (`mpcBld_mWord_four`, `mpcBld_defect_four`).  Every factor of the defect lies in the central
   involutive layer `Z = λ₃/λ₄`, so the class-four rung is an equation in an elementary abelian
   2-group: exact linear algebra, not a search.

2. **The class-four rung is climbed** (§3).  The wave-84 witness `s = t = ⁅D̄, B̄⁆`, `m = n = 1`
   kills the defect (`mpcBld_mem_four_witness`), so `(mpcWordSet 4).Nonempty`
   (`mpcBld_nonempty_four`) and the residue starts at **class five**
   (`mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class_five`).  This turns wave 84 §4.2 from a checked hand
   computation into a theorem.  [W87-FIVE: class five is also climbed (`mpcFv_nonempty_five`,
   witness `mpcFvW5`, `MpcFive.lean`); the residue starts at class SIX.]

3. **The widened shape** (§4).  The `B̄`- and `D̄`-corrections may range over the closed subgroup
   generated by `Ā`, `C̄₀` and the Frattini subgroup (`mpcBldWide`): generation still holds
   (`mpcBld_gen`), so the word identity still gives `MpcPivShift 2`
   (`mpcBld_shift_of_word`), and the per-class criterion transfers verbatim
   (`mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class`, `mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class_five`).  The widened rungs
   below five are free for the same reason the narrow ones are (`mpcBld_wide_nonempty_four`).

   [W86-HOUSE, as of `f0de6ad5`: two name slips in this bullet, both checked by elaboration.
   `mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class_five` is the NARROW criterion (its hypothesis is over
   `mpcWordSet`); the widened one is `mpcBld_wide_shift_of_forall_class_five`, over `mpcBldSet`.
   And `mpcBld_wide_nonempty_four` does not exist; the declaration is
   `mpcBld_wide_nonempty_of_le_four`.  The mathematics of the bullet is right: `mpcWordSet k ⊆
   mpcBldSet k` (`mpcBld_wordSet_subset`), so the widened hypothesis is the weaker one and the
   widened criterion is the stronger theorem.  §4's "strictly more room at every rung" is the
   one word to discount: only the non-strict `mpcWordCorr ≤ mpcBldCorrW` is proved.]

## What does not land

**The decision.**  `MpcPivShift 2` is still neither proved nor refuted.  What moved is the
starting line: wave 84 left the residue at class four with an unformalized witness, and this lane
leaves it at **class five**, with the class-four defect computed exactly rather than sampled.  No
class-five claim is made in either direction; wave 84 §5's control (the greedy ladder kills `M5`,
which is a theorem) still forbids reading any stall as evidence.

Declaration prefix `mpcBld` (namespace `GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcBld`).  No `sorry`, no new
axiom, no `native_decide`, no `maxHeartbeats`, no `maxRecDepth`.
-/

namespace GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcBld

open GQ2 GQ2.Dyadic GQ2.Dyadic.MarkedCore Multiplicative
open GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcPiv GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcOrb GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcWord
open GQ2.Roe.Labute GQ2.Dyadic.SqCore

noncomputable section

/-! ## §1 The class-four calculus for the `M6` letters

Everything here is read in `Q₄ = G/λ₄` for an arbitrary topological group `G`, with
`Y = λ₂/λ₄` (`lambdaImage G 2 4`) and the central involutive layer `Z = λ₃/λ₄`
(`zLayer G 3`).  The committed class-four calculus (`cfour_*`) supplies every step; the four
lemmas below are the four factors of `mWord`. -/

section ClassFour

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]

/-- Moving a central factor one place to the right. -/
private theorem mpcBld_cmove {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {z : Q} (hz : ∀ x : Q, z * x = x * z)
    (x y : Q) : x * z * y = x * y * z := by
  rw [mul_assoc, hz, ← mul_assoc]

/-- A top-layer element commutes with everything. -/
private theorem mpcBld_zcomm {k : ℕ} {z : levelQuot G (k + 1)} (hz : z ∈ zLayer G k)
    (x : levelQuot G (k + 1)) : z * x = x * z := (zLayer_commute hz x).eq

/-- The bracket swap, in any group. -/
private theorem mpcBld_commP_swap {Q : Type*} [Group Q] (x y : Q) :
    commP x y = (commP y x)⁻¹ := by
  simp only [commP]; group

/-- Naturality of the bracket, as a rewrite rule. -/
theorem mpcBld_map_commP {H K : Type*} [Group H] [Group K] (f : H →* K) (x y : H) :
    f (commP x y) = commP (f x) (f y) := by
  simp only [commP, map_mul, map_inv]

/-- **The near slot of a bracket is a homomorphism on `Y`.**  The correction term of
`cfour_commP_mul_left` is a bracket against a `Z`-element. -/
theorem mpcBld_commP_hom_left {y : levelQuot G 4} (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4)
    (y' r : levelQuot G 4) : commP (y * y') r = commP y r * commP y' r := by
  rw [cfour_commP_mul_left, cfour_commP_zLayer_left (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hy r) y', mul_one]

/-- The near slot of a bracket inverts on `Y`. -/
theorem mpcBld_commP_inv_left {y : levelQuot G 4} (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4)
    (r : levelQuot G 4) : commP y⁻¹ r = (commP y r)⁻¹ := by
  have h : commP (y⁻¹ * y) r = commP y⁻¹ r * commP y r :=
    mpcBld_commP_hom_left (Subgroup.inv_mem _ hy) y r
  rw [inv_mul_cancel, cfour_one_comm] at h
  exact mul_eq_one_iff_eq_inv.mp h.symm

/-- **The `Ā`-letter's square**: `(p·z·σ)² = p²·(σ²·⁅σ,p⁆)` for `z` central of the top layer
(the letter's `B̄⁻⁴` factor) and `σ` a `Y`-correction. -/
theorem mpcBld_sq_letA {p σ z : levelQuot G 4} (hσ : σ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4)
    (hz : z ∈ zLayer G 3) : (p * z * σ) ^ 2 = p ^ 2 * (σ ^ 2 * commP σ p) := by
  rw [mpcBld_cmove (mpcBld_zcomm hz) p σ]
  rw [cfour_sq_mul (p * σ) z, zLayer_sq G hz, cfour_commP_zLayer_left hz (p * σ),
    cfour_one_comm, mul_one, mul_one, mul_one]
  rw [cfour_sq_mul p σ, cfour_commP_zLayer_left (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hσ p) σ, mul_one,
    mul_assoc]

/-- **The `Ā`/`B̄` bracket**: `⁅p·z·σ, q·τ⁆ = ⁅p,q⁆·(⁅p,τ⁆·⁅σ,q⁆)`.  Only the two first-order
terms survive; every correction of a correction dies at class four. -/
theorem mpcBld_comm_letAB {p q σ τ z : levelQuot G 4} (hσ : σ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4)
    (hτ : τ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4) (hz : z ∈ zLayer G 3) :
    commP (p * z * σ) (q * τ) = commP p q * (commP p τ * commP σ q) := by
  have h1 : commP (p * z * σ) (q * τ) = commP (p * z * σ) τ * commP (p * z * σ) q := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_right,
      cfour_commP_lambdaTwo (cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo (p * z * σ) q) hτ, mul_one]
  have h2 : commP (p * z * σ) τ = commP p τ := by
    rw [cfour_commP_left_hom (p * z) σ hτ, cfour_commP_lambdaTwo hσ hτ, mul_one,
      cfour_commP_left_hom p z hτ, cfour_commP_zLayer_left hz τ, mul_one]
  have h3 : commP (p * z * σ) q = commP p q * commP σ q := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_left (p * z) σ q,
      cfour_commP_lambdaTwo (cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo (p * z) q) hσ, mul_one,
      cfour_commP_mul_left p z q, cfour_commP_zLayer_right hz (commP p q),
      cfour_commP_zLayer_left hz q, mul_one, mul_one]
  rw [h1, h2, h3, ← mul_assoc,
    mpcBld_zcomm (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_right p hτ) (commP p q), mul_assoc]

/-- **The `C̄₀`-letter's fourth power is blind to the whole shift**: `(q²·r·μ)⁴ = r⁴`.  Both the
`B̄²` prefix and the `Y`-correction contribute only `Z`-squares, and `Z` has exponent two.

[W86-LADDER5: true at THIS carrier (`levelQuot G 4`) and the collapse does NOT lift; at class
five the same power is `r⁴` times four central order-dividing-two extras
(`mpcLad_pow_letC_five`).  Do not conflate with `mpcBld_incr_pivot`, which is class-uniform
and stands.] -/
theorem mpcBld_pow_letC (q r : levelQuot G 4) {μ : levelQuot G 4}
    (hμ : μ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4) : (q ^ 2 * r * μ) ^ 4 = r ^ 4 := by
  have hq2 : q ^ 2 ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4 := cfour_sq_mem_lambdaTwo q
  have hμ4 : μ ^ 4 = 1 := by
    rw [pow_mul μ 2 2]
    exact zLayer_sq G (cfour_sq_mem_zLayer hμ)
  have hq24 : (q ^ 2) ^ 4 = 1 := by
    rw [pow_mul (q ^ 2) 2 2]
    exact zLayer_sq G (cfour_sq_mem_zLayer hq2)
  rw [cfour_pow_four_mul (q ^ 2 * r) μ, hμ4, mul_one,
    zLayer_sq G (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hμ (q ^ 2 * r)), mul_one,
    cfour_pow_four_mul (q ^ 2) r, hq24, one_mul,
    zLayer_sq G (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_right r hq2), mul_one]

/-- **The `C̄₀`/`D̄` bracket, with the class-four obstruction visible**:

    ⁅q²·r·μ, w·ν⁆ = ⁅r,w⁆ · (⁅q,w⁆²·⁅⁅q,w⁆,q⁆·⁅r,ν⁆·⁅μ,w⁆).

The two terms `⁅q,w⁆²·⁅⁅q,w⁆,q⁆` are the `B̄²` prefix's own cost - the Hall-Petrescu expansion of
`⁅q², w⁆` - and they are the whole class-four obstruction of the bare ansatz. -/
theorem mpcBld_comm_letCD {q r w μ ν : levelQuot G 4} (hμ : μ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4)
    (hν : ν ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4) :
    commP (q ^ 2 * r * μ) (w * ν)
      = commP r w * (commP q w ^ 2 * commP (commP q w) q * commP r ν * commP μ w) := by
  have hq2 : q ^ 2 ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4 := cfour_sq_mem_lambdaTwo q
  have hβ : commP q w ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4 := cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo q w
  have hκ : commP (commP q w) q ∈ zLayer G 3 := cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hβ q
  have hβ2 : commP q w ^ 2 ∈ zLayer G 3 := cfour_sq_mem_zLayer hβ
  have hγ : commP r ν ∈ zLayer G 3 := cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_right r hν
  have hδ : commP μ w ∈ zLayer G 3 := cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hμ w
  have h1 : commP (q ^ 2 * r * μ) (w * ν)
      = commP (q ^ 2 * r * μ) ν * commP (q ^ 2 * r * μ) w := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_right,
      cfour_commP_lambdaTwo (cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo (q ^ 2 * r * μ) w) hν, mul_one]
  have h2 : commP (q ^ 2 * r * μ) ν = commP r ν := by
    rw [cfour_commP_left_hom (q ^ 2 * r) μ hν, cfour_commP_lambdaTwo hμ hν, mul_one,
      cfour_commP_left_hom (q ^ 2) r hν, cfour_commP_sq_left q hν, one_mul]
  have h4 : commP (q ^ 2) w = commP q w ^ 2 * commP (commP q w) q := by
    rw [pow_two q, cfour_commP_mul_left q q w, mpcBld_cmove (mpcBld_zcomm hκ), ← pow_two]
  have h3 : commP (q ^ 2 * r * μ) w
      = commP q w ^ 2 * commP (commP q w) q * commP r w * commP μ w := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_left (q ^ 2 * r) μ w,
      cfour_commP_lambdaTwo (cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo (q ^ 2 * r) w) hμ, mul_one,
      cfour_commP_mul_left (q ^ 2) r w,
      cfour_commP_zLayer_left (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hq2 w) r, mul_one, h4]
  rw [h1, h2, h3]
  simp only [← mul_assoc]
  rw [mpcBld_zcomm hγ (commP q w ^ 2), mpcBld_cmove (mpcBld_zcomm hγ) (commP q w ^ 2),
    mpcBld_cmove (mpcBld_zcomm hγ) (commP q w ^ 2 * commP (commP q w) q),
    mpcBld_cmove (mpcBld_zcomm hκ) (commP q w ^ 2),
    mpcBld_zcomm hβ2 (commP r w)]

/-- The four-fold central shuffle used to assemble the core word. -/
private theorem mpcBld_shuffle4 {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {z₁ z₂ z₄ : Q}
    (h₁ : ∀ x : Q, z₁ * x = x * z₁) (h₂ : ∀ x : Q, z₂ * x = x * z₂) (x₁ x₂ x₃ x₄ : Q) :
    x₁ * z₁ * (x₂ * z₂) * x₃ * (x₄ * z₄) = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * (z₁ * z₂ * z₄) := by
  have e₁ := mpcBld_cmove h₁
  have e₂ := mpcBld_cmove h₂
  calc x₁ * z₁ * (x₂ * z₂) * x₃ * (x₄ * z₄)
      = x₁ * z₁ * x₂ * z₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z₄ := by group
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * z₁ * z₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z₄ := by rw [e₁ x₁ x₂]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * z₁ * x₃ * z₂ * x₄ * z₄ := by rw [e₂ (x₁ * x₂ * z₁) x₃]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z₁ * z₂ * x₄ * z₄ := by rw [e₁ (x₁ * x₂) x₃]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z₁ * x₄ * z₂ * z₄ := by rw [e₂ (x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z₁) x₄]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z₁ * z₂ * z₄ := by rw [e₁ (x₁ * x₂ * x₃) x₄]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * (z₁ * z₂ * z₄) := by group

/-- ⭐⭐ **THE CLASS-FOUR DEFECT OF THE `M6` ANSATZ, IN CLOSED FORM.**  In `Q₄`, for any four
`Y`-corrections,

    mWord 2 (p·z·σ) (q·τ) (q²·r·μ) (w·ν)
      = mWord 2 p q r w · (σ²·⁅σ,p⁆ · ⁅p,τ⁆·⁅σ,q⁆ · ⁅q,w⁆²·⁅⁅q,w⁆,q⁆·⁅r,ν⁆·⁅μ,w⁆)

with `z` any element of the top layer (the ansatz uses `z = (q⁴)⁻¹`).  Every factor of the
defect lies in `Z`, which is central of exponent two, so **the class-four rung is a linear
equation over `𝔽₂`**: this is the exact per-class statement the greedy ladder can only sample. -/
theorem mpcBld_mWord_four {p q r w σ τ μ ν z : levelQuot G 4}
    (hσ : σ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4) (hτ : τ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4)
    (hμ : μ ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4) (hν : ν ∈ lambdaImage G 2 4) (hz : z ∈ zLayer G 3) :
    mWord 2 (p * z * σ) (q * τ) (q ^ 2 * r * μ) (w * ν)
      = mWord 2 p q r w * (σ ^ 2 * commP σ p * (commP p τ * commP σ q) *
          (commP q w ^ 2 * commP (commP q w) q * commP r ν * commP μ w)) := by
  have hE₁ : σ ^ 2 * commP σ p ∈ zLayer G 3 :=
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ (cfour_sq_mem_zLayer hσ) (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hσ p)
  have hE₂ : commP p τ * commP σ q ∈ zLayer G 3 :=
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_right p hτ) (cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hσ q)
  simp only [mWord, show (2 : ℕ) ^ 2 = 4 from rfl]
  rw [mpcBld_sq_letA hσ hz, mpcBld_comm_letAB hσ hτ hz, mpcBld_pow_letC q r hμ,
    mpcBld_comm_letCD hμ hν]
  exact mpcBld_shuffle4 (z₄ := _) (mpcBld_zcomm hE₁) (mpcBld_zcomm hE₂) _ _ _ _

end ClassFour

/-! ## §2 The defect downstairs, on `D_M 2 0`

Transporting §1 through `levelMk` and killing the marked relator with `mpcOrb_relation`: the
whole class-four content of the `M6` ansatz is that one eight-term product dies. -/

section Defect

/-- The `M6` ansatz's core word, modulo `λ₄`, is exactly the defect. -/
theorem mpcBld_defect_four (s t m n : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hs : s ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2)
    (ht : t ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2)
    (hm : m ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2)
    (hn : n ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2) :
    levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n))
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4
        (s ^ 2 * commP s (dmA 2 0) * (commP (dmA 2 0) t * commP s (dmB 2 0)) *
          (commP (dmB 2 0) (dmD 2 0) ^ 2 * commP (commP (dmB 2 0) (dmD 2 0)) (dmB 2 0) *
            commP (dmC 2 0) n * commP m (dmD 2 0))) := by
  have hrel : mWord 2 (levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmA 2 0)) (levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmB 2 0))
      (levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmC 2 0)) (levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmD 2 0)) = 1 := by
    rw [← map_mWord, mpcOrb_relation, map_one]
  have hz : (levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmB 2 0) ^ 4)⁻¹ ∈ zLayer (DM 2 0 : Type) 3 :=
    Subgroup.inv_mem _ (cfour_pow_four_mem_zLayer _)
  have hA : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (mpcWordLetA s)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmA 2 0) * (levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmB 2 0) ^ 4)⁻¹ *
        levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 s := by
    rw [mpcWordLetA, map_mul, map_mul, map_inv, map_pow]
  have hB : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (mpcWordLetB t)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmB 2 0) * levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 t := by
    rw [mpcWordLetB, map_mul]
  have hC : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (mpcWordLetC m)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmB 2 0) ^ 2 * levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmC 2 0) *
        levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 m := by
    rw [mpcWordLetC, map_mul, map_mul, map_pow]
  have hD : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (mpcWordLetD n)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmD 2 0) * levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 n := by
    rw [mpcWordLetD, map_mul]
  rw [map_mWord, hA, hB, hC, hD,
    mpcBld_mWord_four (G := (DM 2 0 : Type)) ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩ ⟨t, ht, rfl⟩ ⟨m, hm, rfl⟩ ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
      hz, hrel, one_mul]
  simp only [map_mul, map_pow, commP, map_inv]

end Defect

/-! ## §3 The class-four rung, climbed

Wave 84 §4.2's witness `s = t = ⁅D̄, B̄⁆`, `m = n = 1` kills the defect: the `⁅D̄,B̄⁆`-square
cancels `⁅B̄,D̄⁆²`, the two `Ā`-brackets cancel each other, and `⁅⁅D̄,B̄⁆,B̄⁆` cancels the triple
bracket `⁅⁅B̄,D̄⁆,B̄⁆`.  All six live in the exponent-two layer `Z`, so the cancellation is the
elementary abelian one, and the hand computation becomes a theorem. -/

section Witness

/-- Six central involutions in the pattern the witness produces multiply to `1`. -/
private theorem mpcBld_kill6 {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {z₁ z₂ z₃ : Q}
    (h₁ : ∀ x : Q, z₁ * x = x * z₁) (e₁ : z₁ ^ 2 = 1) (e₂ : z₂ ^ 2 = 1) (e₃ : z₃ ^ 2 = 1) :
    z₁ * z₂ * (z₂ * z₃) * (z₁ * z₃) = 1 := by
  calc z₁ * z₂ * (z₂ * z₃) * (z₁ * z₃)
      = z₁ * z₂ * (z₂ * z₃) * z₁ * z₃ := by group
    _ = z₁ * (z₁ * z₂ * (z₂ * z₃)) * z₃ := by rw [← h₁ (z₁ * z₂ * (z₂ * z₃))]
    _ = z₁ ^ 2 * z₂ ^ 2 * z₃ ^ 2 := by rw [pow_two, pow_two, pow_two]; group
    _ = 1 := by rw [e₁, e₂, e₃, one_mul, one_mul]

/-- The `M6` witness correction: `⁅D̄, B̄⁆`. -/
def mpcBldW : (DM 2 0 : Type) := commP (dmD 2 0) (dmB 2 0)

theorem mpcBld_w_mem : mpcBldW ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 :=
  cfour_commP_mem_two _ _

/-- Every bracket is χ-trivial: `χ_M` lands in the commutative group `ℤ₂ˣ`. -/
theorem mpcBld_chi_commP (x y : (DM 2 0 : Type)) : chiM 2 0 (commP x y) = 1 := by
  have h : chiM 2 0 (commP x y)
      = (chiM 2 0 x)⁻¹ * (chiM 2 0 y)⁻¹ * chiM 2 0 x * chiM 2 0 y := by
    simp only [commP, map_mul, map_inv]
  rw [h, mul_comm ((chiM 2 0 x)⁻¹) ((chiM 2 0 y)⁻¹)]
  group

/-- ⭐⭐ **THE CLASS-FOUR RUNG IS CLIMBED.**  The wave-84 witness `s = t = ⁅D̄, B̄⁆`, `m = n = 1`
solves the `M6` identity to class four.  Formalizes wave 84 §4.2, whose kill was a hand
computation in the Magnus model. -/
theorem mpcBld_mem_four_witness :
    mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA mpcBldW) (mpcWordLetB mpcBldW) (mpcWordLetC 1) (mpcWordLetD 1)
      ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 := by
  rw [mpcWord_mem_iff_levelMk,
    mpcBld_defect_four mpcBldW mpcBldW 1 1 mpcBld_w_mem mpcBld_w_mem (one_mem _) (one_mem _)]
  simp only [mpcBldW, map_mul, map_pow, mpcBld_map_commP, cfour_comm_one,
    cfour_one_comm, mul_one]
  set p := levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmA 2 0) with hp
  set q := levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmB 2 0) with hq
  set r := levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmC 2 0) with hr
  set w := levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) 4 (dmD 2 0) with hw
  have hβ : commP q w ∈ lambdaImage (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 4 := cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo q w
  have hβinv : commP w q ∈ lambdaImage (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 4 := cfour_commP_mem_lambdaTwo w q
  have hβ2 : commP q w ^ 2 ∈ zLayer (DM 2 0 : Type) 3 := cfour_sq_mem_zLayer hβ
  have hκ : commP (commP q w) q ∈ zLayer (DM 2 0 : Type) 3 :=
    cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hβ q
  have hP : commP (commP w q) p ∈ zLayer (DM 2 0 : Type) 3 :=
    cfour_commP_mem_zLayer_left hβinv p
  -- the three cancellations
  have hsq : commP w q ^ 2 = commP q w ^ 2 := by
    rw [mpcBld_commP_swap w q, inv_pow]
    exact zLayer_inv_self hβ2
  have hswapA : commP p (commP w q) = commP (commP w q) p := by
    rw [mpcBld_commP_swap p (commP w q)]
    exact zLayer_inv_self hP
  have hswapB : commP (commP w q) q = commP (commP q w) q := by
    rw [mpcBld_commP_swap w q, mpcBld_commP_inv_left hβ q]
    exact zLayer_inv_self hκ
  rw [hsq, hswapA, hswapB]
  exact mpcBld_kill6 (mpcBld_zcomm hβ2) (zLayer_sq _ hβ2)
    (zLayer_sq _ hP) (zLayer_sq _ hκ)

/-- The class-four solution set of the `M6` ansatz is nonempty. -/
theorem mpcBld_nonempty_four : (mpcWordSet 4).Nonempty := by
  refine ⟨(mpcBldW, mpcBldW, 1, 1), ⟨mpcBld_w_mem, ?_⟩, ⟨mpcBld_w_mem, ?_⟩, one_mem _,
    one_mem _, mpcBld_mem_four_witness⟩ <;>
  exact mpcBld_chi_commP _ _

/-- ⭐ **THE RESIDUE STARTS AT CLASS FIVE.**  Wave 84's `mpcWord_shift_of_forall_class_four` with
its first rung discharged: `MpcPivShift 2` follows from class-`k` solvability for `k ≥ 5` alone. -/
theorem mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class_five
    (H : ∀ k, 5 ≤ k → (mpcWordSet k).Nonempty) : MpcPivShift 2 := by
  refine mpcWord_shift_of_forall_class_four fun k hk => ?_
  rcases eq_or_lt_of_le hk with h | h
  · exact h ▸ mpcBld_nonempty_four
  · exact H k (by omega)

end Witness

/-! ## §4 The widened shape

`MpcPivShift` constrains only the `C̄₀` row, so the `B̄`- and `D̄`-letters may carry any factor
the four χ-values tolerate.  Modulo the Frattini subgroup the χ-trivial marked generators are
`Ā` and `C̄₀`, so the widened carrier is the closed subgroup they generate together with the
Frattini subgroup itself.  Generation survives (the four images still span `𝔽₂⁴`: `Ā` and `C̄₀`
are recovered from the `Ā`- and `C̄₀`-letters first, and then the widened factors of the `B̄`- and
`D̄`-letters are already in the subgroup), so the widened shape is a valid route to
`MpcPivShift 2` with strictly more room at every rung. -/

section Widened

/-- The widened correction carrier for the `B̄`- and `D̄`-slots: the closed subgroup generated by
`Ā`, `C̄₀` and the Frattini subgroup. -/
def mpcBldWide : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type) :=
  (Subgroup.closure ({dmA 2 0, dmC 2 0} : Set (DM 2 0 : Type)) ⊔ mpcWordFrat).topologicalClosure

theorem mpcBld_isClosed_wide :
    IsClosed ((mpcBldWide : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type)) : Set (DM 2 0 : Type)) :=
  Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _

theorem mpcBld_frat_le_wide : mpcWordFrat ≤ mpcBldWide :=
  le_trans le_sup_right (Subgroup.le_topologicalClosure _)

theorem mpcBld_lambdaTwo_le_wide : twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 ≤ mpcBldWide :=
  le_trans mpcWord_lambdaTwo_le_frat mpcBld_frat_le_wide

/-- An index-two open normal subgroup containing `Ā` and `C̄₀` contains the whole widened
carrier: it contains the Frattini subgroup for free, and it is closed. -/
theorem mpcBld_wide_le {M : OpenNormalSubgroup (DM 2 0 : Type)} (hM : M.toSubgroup.index = 2)
    (hA : dmA 2 0 ∈ M.toSubgroup) (hC : dmC 2 0 ∈ M.toSubgroup) :
    mpcBldWide ≤ M.toSubgroup := by
  refine Subgroup.topologicalClosure_minimal _ (sup_le ?_ ?_) M.toOpenSubgroup.isClosed
  · rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro x (rfl | rfl)
    exacts [hA, hC]
  · exact fun x hx => (mpcWord_mem_frat_iff.mp hx) M hM

/-- ⭐ **THE WIDENED ANSATZ GENERATES.**  With the `Ā`- and `C̄₀`-corrections Frattini and the
`B̄`- and `D̄`-corrections in the widened carrier, the four letters still topologically generate
`D_M 2 0`.  The order of the Frattini argument matters: `Ā` and `C̄₀` come out of their own
letters first, and only then do the widened factors of the other two become available. -/
theorem mpcBld_gen (s t m n : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hs : s ∈ mpcWordFrat) (ht : t ∈ mpcBldWide) (hm : m ∈ mpcWordFrat) (hn : n ∈ mpcBldWide) :
    (Subgroup.closure ({mpcWordLetA s, mpcWordLetB t, mpcWordLetC m, mpcWordLetD n} :
      Set (DM 2 0 : Type))).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := by
  haveI : Fact (Nat.Prime 2) := ⟨Nat.prime_two⟩
  refine eq_top_of_forall_not_le_index_p (p := 2) (isProP_DM 2 0)
    (Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _) ?_
  intro M hM hle
  have hsub : Subgroup.closure ({mpcWordLetA s, mpcWordLetB t, mpcWordLetC m, mpcWordLetD n} :
      Set (DM 2 0 : Type)) ≤ M.toSubgroup :=
    le_trans (Subgroup.le_topologicalClosure _) hle
  have hmemA : mpcWordLetA s ∈ M.toSubgroup :=
    hsub (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl rfl))
  have hmemB : mpcWordLetB t ∈ M.toSubgroup :=
    hsub (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl)))
  have hmemC : mpcWordLetC m ∈ M.toSubgroup :=
    hsub (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl))))
  have hmemD : mpcWordLetD n ∈ M.toSubgroup :=
    hsub (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr rfl))))
  have hsM : s ∈ M.toSubgroup := (mpcWord_mem_frat_iff.mp hs) M hM
  have hmM : m ∈ M.toSubgroup := (mpcWord_mem_frat_iff.mp hm) M hM
  have hB2 : dmB 2 0 ^ 2 ∈ M.toSubgroup :=
    (mpcWord_mem_frat_iff.mp (mpcWord_sq_mem (dmB 2 0))) M hM
  have hB4 : dmB 2 0 ^ 4 ∈ M.toSubgroup := by
    have h : dmB 2 0 ^ 4 = (dmB 2 0 ^ 2) ^ 2 := by rw [← pow_mul]
    rw [h]
    exact (mpcWord_mem_frat_iff.mp (mpcWord_sq_mem (dmB 2 0 ^ 2))) M hM
  have hA : dmA 2 0 ∈ M.toSubgroup := by
    have h : dmA 2 0 = mpcWordLetA s * s⁻¹ * dmB 2 0 ^ 4 := by rw [mpcWordLetA]; group
    rw [h]
    exact M.toSubgroup.mul_mem (M.toSubgroup.mul_mem hmemA (M.toSubgroup.inv_mem hsM)) hB4
  have hC : dmC 2 0 ∈ M.toSubgroup := by
    have h : dmC 2 0 = (dmB 2 0 ^ 2)⁻¹ * mpcWordLetC m * m⁻¹ := by rw [mpcWordLetC]; group
    rw [h]
    exact M.toSubgroup.mul_mem
      (M.toSubgroup.mul_mem (M.toSubgroup.inv_mem hB2) hmemC) (M.toSubgroup.inv_mem hmM)
  have htM : t ∈ M.toSubgroup := mpcBld_wide_le hM hA hC ht
  have hnM : n ∈ M.toSubgroup := mpcBld_wide_le hM hA hC hn
  have hB : dmB 2 0 ∈ M.toSubgroup := by
    have h : dmB 2 0 = mpcWordLetB t * t⁻¹ := by rw [mpcWordLetB]; group
    rw [h]
    exact M.toSubgroup.mul_mem hmemB (M.toSubgroup.inv_mem htM)
  have hD : dmD 2 0 ∈ M.toSubgroup := by
    have h : dmD 2 0 = mpcWordLetD n * n⁻¹ := by rw [mpcWordLetD]; group
    rw [h]
    exact M.toSubgroup.mul_mem hmemD (M.toSubgroup.inv_mem hnM)
  have hgens : Subgroup.closure (Set.range (dmGen 2 0)) ≤ M.toSubgroup := by
    rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    fin_cases i
    exacts [hA, hB, hC, hD]
  have htop : (⊤ : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type)) ≤ M.toSubgroup := by
    rw [← dm_topGen 2 0]
    exact Subgroup.topologicalClosure_minimal _ hgens M.toOpenSubgroup.isClosed
  have hMtop : M.toSubgroup = ⊤ := top_le_iff.mp htop
  rw [hMtop, Subgroup.index_top] at hM
  exact absurd hM (by norm_num)

/-- ⭐ **THE WIDENED WORD CRITERION.**  Wave 84's `mpcWord_shift_of_word` with the `B̄`- and
`D̄`-corrections widened: the single identity still yields `MpcPivShift 2`, hence the tied `√−10`
branch datum with no clause. -/
theorem mpcBld_shift_of_word (s t m n : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hs : s ∈ mpcWordFrat) (ht : t ∈ mpcBldWide) (hm : m ∈ mpcWordFrat)
    (hn : n ∈ mpcBldWide)
    (hchis : chiM 2 0 s = 1) (hchit : chiM 2 0 t = 1) (hchim : chiM 2 0 m = 1)
    (hchin : chiM 2 0 n = 1)
    (hmrow : ∀ f : ContinuousMonoidHom (DM 2 0 : Type) (Multiplicative ℤ_[2]), f m = 1)
    (hrel : mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n) = 1) :
    MpcPivShift 2 := by
  have h4 : ((-1 : ℤ_[2]ˣ)) ^ 4 = 1 := by
    rw [show (4 : ℕ) = 2 * 2 from rfl, pow_mul, neg_one_sq, one_pow]
  refine mpcOrb_shift_of_marking hrel (mpcBld_gen s t m n hs ht hm hn) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rw [mpcWordLetA, map_mul, map_mul, map_inv, map_pow, chiM_dmA, chiM_dmB, hchis, h4]
    simp
  · rw [mpcWordLetB, map_mul, chiM_dmB, hchit, mul_one]
  · rw [mpcWordLetC, map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, chiM_dmB, chiM_dmC, hchim, neg_one_sq]
    simp
  · rw [mpcWordLetD, map_mul, chiM_dmD, hchin, mul_one]
  · intro f
    have hC : mpcWordLetC m = dmB 2 0 * dmB 2 0 * dmC 2 0 * m := by rw [mpcWordLetC, sq]
    have hfC : f (mpcWordLetC m) = f (dmB 2 0) * f (dmB 2 0) * f (dmC 2 0) := by
      rw [hC, map_mul, map_mul, map_mul, hmrow f, mul_one]
    rw [hfC, toAdd_mul, toAdd_mul]
    ring

/-- The widened correction carrier for the `B̄`- and `D̄`-slots, with the χ-value imposed. -/
def mpcBldCorrW : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type) := mpcBldWide ⊓ (chiM 2 0).toMonoidHom.ker

theorem mpcBld_corr_le_corrW : mpcWordCorr ≤ mpcBldCorrW :=
  inf_le_inf (le_trans mpcWord_lambdaTwo_le_frat mpcBld_frat_le_wide) le_rfl

/-- **The widened class-`k` solution set.**  Only the `B̄`- and `D̄`-slots move; the `Ā`-slot and
the pivot slot carry wave 84's carriers unchanged. -/
def mpcBldSet (k : ℕ) :
    Set ((DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type)) :=
  {p | p.1 ∈ mpcWordCorr ∧ p.2.1 ∈ mpcBldCorrW ∧ p.2.2.1 ∈ mpcWordCorrC ∧
    p.2.2.2 ∈ mpcBldCorrW ∧
      mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA p.1) (mpcWordLetB p.2.1) (mpcWordLetC p.2.2.1)
          (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) k}

theorem mpcBldSet_antitone {k k' : ℕ} (hkk : k' ≤ k) : mpcBldSet k ⊆ mpcBldSet k' :=
  fun _ ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5⟩ =>
    ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, twoCentralSeries_antitone (G := (DM 2 0 : Type)) hkk h5⟩

/-- The narrow solution sets sit inside the widened ones. -/
theorem mpcBld_wordSet_subset (k : ℕ) : mpcWordSet k ⊆ mpcBldSet k :=
  fun _ ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5⟩ => ⟨h1, mpcBld_corr_le_corrW h2, h3, mpcBld_corr_le_corrW h4, h5⟩

theorem mpcBld_isClosed_corrW : IsClosed ((mpcBldCorrW : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type)) :
    Set (DM 2 0 : Type)) := by
  have h2 : IsClosed (((chiM 2 0).toMonoidHom.ker : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type)) :
      Set (DM 2 0 : Type)) := by
    have h : (((chiM 2 0).toMonoidHom.ker : Subgroup (DM 2 0 : Type)) : Set (DM 2 0 : Type))
        = {x | chiM 2 0 x = 1} := rfl
    rw [h]
    exact isClosed_eq (chiM 2 0).continuous_toFun continuous_const
  exact mpcBld_isClosed_wide.inter h2

theorem mpcBld_isClosed_set (k : ℕ) : IsClosed (mpcBldSet k) := by
  have hA : IsClosed {p : (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) ×
      (DM 2 0 : Type) | p.1 ∈ mpcWordCorr} :=
    mpcWord_isClosed_corr.preimage continuous_fst
  have hB : IsClosed {p : (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) ×
      (DM 2 0 : Type) | p.2.1 ∈ mpcBldCorrW} :=
    mpcBld_isClosed_corrW.preimage (continuous_fst.comp continuous_snd)
  have hC : IsClosed {p : (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) ×
      (DM 2 0 : Type) | p.2.2.1 ∈ mpcWordCorrC} :=
    mpcWord_isClosed_corrC.preimage (continuous_fst.comp (continuous_snd.comp continuous_snd))
  have hD : IsClosed {p : (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) ×
      (DM 2 0 : Type) | p.2.2.2 ∈ mpcBldCorrW} :=
    mpcBld_isClosed_corrW.preimage (continuous_snd.comp (continuous_snd.comp continuous_snd))
  exact hA.inter (hB.inter (hC.inter (hD.inter
    ((isClosed_twoCentralSeries (G := (DM 2 0 : Type)) k).preimage mpcWord_continuous))))

/-- ⭐ **THE WIDENED PER-CLASS CRITERION.**  Wave 84's compactness assembly, verbatim, over the
widened carriers: class-`k` solvability for every `k` gives `MpcPivShift 2`.  Contrapositively,
the widened shape also fails at a finite class if it fails at all. -/
theorem mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class (H : ∀ k, (mpcBldSet k).Nonempty) : MpcPivShift 2 := by
  have hne : (⋂ k, mpcBldSet k).Nonempty := by
    apply IsCompact.nonempty_iInter_of_directed_nonempty_isCompact_isClosed
    · exact fun k k' => ⟨max k k', mpcBldSet_antitone (le_max_left k k'),
        mpcBldSet_antitone (le_max_right k k')⟩
    · exact H
    · exact fun k => (mpcBld_isClosed_set k).isCompact
    · exact fun k => mpcBld_isClosed_set k
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hne
  have hmem : ∀ k, p ∈ mpcBldSet k := Set.mem_iInter.mp hp
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, -⟩ := hmem 0
  have hall : mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA p.1) (mpcWordLetB p.2.1) (mpcWordLetC p.2.2.1)
      (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) ∈ ⨅ k, twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) k :=
    Subgroup.mem_iInf.mpr fun k => (hmem k).2.2.2.2
  rw [mpcWord_iInf_twoCentralSeries, Subgroup.mem_bot] at hall
  exact mpcBld_shift_of_word p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2
    (mpcWord_lambdaTwo_le_frat h1.1) h2.1 (mpcWord_lambdaTwo_le_frat h3.1.1) h4.1
    h1.2 h2.2 h3.1.2 h4.2 (fun f => (mpcWord_mem_rowKer.mp h3.2) f) hall

/-- The widened rungs at most four are climbed, by the narrow witness. -/
theorem mpcBld_wide_nonempty_of_le_four {k : ℕ} (hk : k ≤ 4) : (mpcBldSet k).Nonempty := by
  refine Set.Nonempty.mono (mpcBld_wordSet_subset k) ?_
  by_cases h : k ≤ 3
  · exact mpcWord_nonempty_of_le_three h
  · exact Set.Nonempty.mono (mpcWordSet_antitone (by omega : k ≤ 4)) mpcBld_nonempty_four

/-- ⭐ **THE WIDENED RESIDUE STARTS AT CLASS FIVE.** -/
theorem mpcBld_wide_shift_of_forall_class_five
    (H : ∀ k, 5 ≤ k → (mpcBldSet k).Nonempty) : MpcPivShift 2 := by
  refine mpcBld_shift_of_forall_class fun k => ?_
  by_cases hk : 5 ≤ k
  · exact H k hk
  · exact mpcBld_wide_nonempty_of_le_four (by omega)

end Widened

/-! ## §5 The increment engine: what one rung of the ladder actually costs

Wave 84 §6's structural remark - each rung is a *single* linear condition, because the Fox ideal
of the relator is the χ-twisted augmentation kernel - is here in the only form a builder can use:
an exact, class-uniform description of what each correction slot buys.

Changing the `B̄`-correction by `u ∈ λ_j` multiplies the core word by `⁅Ā, u⁆` modulo `λ_{j+2}`,
**exactly**, whatever the other three corrections are; changing the `D̄`-correction by `u` buys
`⁅C̄₀, u⁆` on the same terms.  Both maps are homomorphisms into the elementary abelian layer
`λ_{j+1}/λ_{j+2}`, so the reachable increments form an `𝔽₂`-subspace and every rung above four is
the linear question **"is the defect in `⁅Ā, λ_j ∩ ker χ_M⁆ · ⁅C̄₀, λ_j ∩ ker χ_M⁆?"**.  That is
the closed form the greedy ladder was only sampling. -/

section Increment

section IncrGeneral

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G] {j : ℕ}

/-- Every bracket of `Q_{j+2}` lies in the `λ₂`-image. -/
private theorem mpcBld_commP_mem_two (p q : levelQuot G (j + 2)) :
    commP p q ∈ lambdaImage G 2 (j + 2) := by
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := levelMk_surjective G (j + 2) p
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := levelMk_surjective G (j + 2) q
  exact ⟨commP a b, cfour_commP_mem_two a b, by simp only [commP, map_mul, map_inv]⟩

/-- `⁅λ₂, λ_j⁆` dies in `Q_{j+2}`. -/
private theorem mpcBld_vanish {y ε : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 (j + 2)) (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) : commP y ε = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩ := hy
  obtain ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩ := hε
  have h : commP (levelMk G (j + 2) v) (levelMk G (j + 2) w)
      = levelMk G (j + 2) (commP v w) := by simp only [commP, map_mul, map_inv]
  rw [h]
  exact (lim_mem_twoCentralSeries_iff_levelMk (j + 2) _).mp
    (cfive_commutator_lambdaTwo_swap hw hv)

/-- `⁅λ_j, λ₂⁆` dies in `Q_{j+2}`, the slots the other way round. -/
private theorem mpcBld_vanish' {y ε : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 (j + 2)) (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) : commP ε y = 1 := by
  have h : commP ε y = (commP y ε)⁻¹ := by simp only [commP]; group
  rw [h, mpcBld_vanish hy hε, inv_one]

/-- The square of a `λ_j`-image lands in the top layer of `Q_{j+2}`. -/
private theorem mpcBld_sq_mem_zLayer {ε : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) : ε ^ 2 ∈ zLayer G (j + 1) := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩ := hε
  exact ⟨v ^ 2, sq_mem_twoCentralSeries_succ G hv, by rw [map_pow]⟩

private theorem mpcBld_cmove3 {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {z : Q} (hz : ∀ x : Q, z * x = x * z)
    (x₁ x₂ x₃ x₄ : Q) : x₁ * (z * x₂) * x₃ * x₄ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z := by
  have e := mpcBld_cmove hz
  calc x₁ * (z * x₂) * x₃ * x₄ = x₁ * z * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ := by group
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * z * x₃ * x₄ := by rw [e x₁ x₂]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z * x₄ := by rw [e (x₁ * x₂) x₃]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z := by rw [e (x₁ * x₂ * x₃) x₄]

private theorem mpcBld_cmove4 {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {z : Q} (hz : ∀ x : Q, z * x = x * z)
    (x₁ x₂ x₃ x₄ : Q) : x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * (z * x₄) = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z := by
  have e := mpcBld_cmove hz
  calc x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * (z * x₄) = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z * x₄ := by group
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z := by rw [e (x₁ * x₂ * x₃) x₄]

/-- ⭐⭐ **The far slot's increment**: a `λ_j`-factor on the `B̄`-letter costs exactly `⁅Ā, u⁆`
in `Q_{j+2}`, whatever the other three letters are.  The `Ā`-letter's own correction is
invisible: only its leading marked generator survives the bracket. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_far {A α β γ δ ε y : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hα : α = A * y) (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 (j + 2))
    (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) :
    mWord 2 α (β * ε) γ δ = mWord 2 α β γ δ * commP A ε := by
  have h1 : commP α (β * ε) = commP A ε * commP α β := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_right, mpcBld_vanish (mpcBld_commP_mem_two α β) hε, mul_one, hα,
      cfive_commP_left_hom A y hε, mpcBld_vanish hy hε, mul_one]
  simp only [mWord]
  rw [h1]
  exact mpcBld_cmove3 (mpcBld_zcomm (cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_right A hε)) _ _ _ _

/-- ⭐⭐ **The near slot's increment**: a `λ_j`-factor on the `D̄`-letter costs exactly
`⁅C̄₀, u⁆` in `Q_{j+2}`. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_near {C α β γ δ ε y : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hγ : γ = C * y) (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 (j + 2))
    (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) :
    mWord 2 α β γ (δ * ε) = mWord 2 α β γ δ * commP C ε := by
  have h1 : commP γ (δ * ε) = commP C ε * commP γ δ := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_right, mpcBld_vanish (mpcBld_commP_mem_two γ δ) hε, mul_one, hγ,
      cfive_commP_left_hom C y hε, mpcBld_vanish hy hε, mul_one]
  simp only [mWord]
  rw [h1]
  exact mpcBld_cmove4 (mpcBld_zcomm (cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_right C hε)) _ _ _ _

private theorem mpcBld_shuffle3 {Q : Type*} [Group Q] {z₁ z₂ : Q}
    (h₁ : ∀ x : Q, z₁ * x = x * z₁) (h₂ : ∀ x : Q, z₂ * x = x * z₂) (x₁ x₂ x₃ x₄ : Q) :
    x₁ * z₁ * (x₂ * z₂) * x₃ * x₄ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * (z₁ * z₂) := by
  have e₁ := mpcBld_cmove h₁
  have e₂ := mpcBld_cmove h₂
  calc x₁ * z₁ * (x₂ * z₂) * x₃ * x₄ = x₁ * z₁ * x₂ * z₂ * x₃ * x₄ := by group
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * z₁ * z₂ * x₃ * x₄ := by rw [e₁ x₁ x₂]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * z₁ * x₃ * z₂ * x₄ := by rw [e₂ (x₁ * x₂ * z₁) x₃]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z₁ * z₂ * x₄ := by rw [e₁ (x₁ * x₂) x₃]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z₁ * x₄ * z₂ := by rw [e₂ (x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * z₁) x₄]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * z₁ * z₂ := by rw [e₁ (x₁ * x₂ * x₃) x₄]
    _ = x₁ * x₂ * x₃ * x₄ * (z₁ * z₂) := by group

/-- ⭐⭐ **The head slot's increment**: a `λ_j`-factor on the `Ā`-letter costs
`u²·⁅u, Ā⁆·⁅u, b⁆` in `Q_{j+2}`, where `b` is the `B̄`-letter as it stands.  Unlike the two
bracket slots this one sees the `B̄`-letter, which is why it is stated against `β` and not
against a marked generator. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_head {A α β γ δ ε y : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hα : α = A * y) (hy : y ∈ lambdaImage G 2 (j + 2))
    (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) :
    mWord 2 (α * ε) β γ δ = mWord 2 α β γ δ * (ε ^ 2 * commP ε A * commP ε β) := by
  have hεα : commP ε α = commP ε A := by
    rw [hα, cfive_commP_right_hom hε A y, mpcBld_vanish' hy hε, one_mul]
  have hsq : (α * ε) ^ 2 = α ^ 2 * (ε ^ 2 * commP ε A) := by
    rw [cfour_sq_mul, cfive_commP_zLayer_left (cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_left hε α) ε, mul_one,
      hεα, mul_assoc]
  have hcomm : commP (α * ε) β = commP α β * commP ε β := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_left, mpcBld_vanish (mpcBld_commP_mem_two α β) hε, mul_one]
  simp only [mWord]
  rw [hsq, hcomm]
  exact mpcBld_shuffle3
    (mpcBld_zcomm (Subgroup.mul_mem _ (mpcBld_sq_mem_zLayer hε)
      (hεα ▸ cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_left hε α)))
    (mpcBld_zcomm (cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_left hε β)) _ _ _ _

/-- ⭐⭐ **The pivot slot's increment**: a `λ_j`-factor on the `C̄₀`-letter costs exactly
`⁅u, d⁆` in `Q_{j+2}`, where `d` is the `D̄`-letter as it stands.  The fourth power does not
see it at all. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_pivot {α β γ δ ε : levelQuot G (j + 2)}
    (hε : ε ∈ lambdaImage G j (j + 2)) :
    mWord 2 α β (γ * ε) δ = mWord 2 α β γ δ * commP ε δ := by
  have hz : ε ^ 2 * commP ε γ ∈ zLayer G (j + 1) :=
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ (mpcBld_sq_mem_zLayer hε) (cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_left hε γ)
  have hsq : (γ * ε) ^ 2 = γ ^ 2 * (ε ^ 2 * commP ε γ) := by
    rw [cfour_sq_mul, cfive_commP_zLayer_left (cfive_commP_mem_zLayer_left hε γ) ε, mul_one,
      mul_assoc]
  have hfour : (γ * ε) ^ 4 = γ ^ 4 := by
    rw [pow_mul (γ * ε) 2 2, hsq, cfour_sq_mul, zLayer_sq G hz,
      cfive_commP_zLayer_left hz (γ ^ 2), cfour_one_comm, mul_one, mul_one, mul_one,
      ← pow_mul]
  have hcomm : commP (γ * ε) δ = commP γ δ * commP ε δ := by
    rw [cfour_commP_mul_left, mpcBld_vanish (mpcBld_commP_mem_two γ δ) hε, mul_one]
  simp only [mWord, show (2 : ℕ) ^ 2 = 4 from rfl]
  rw [hfour, hcomm, ← mul_assoc]

end IncrGeneral

/-- The `Ā`-letter is the marked `Ā` times a `λ₂`-element. -/
theorem mpcBld_letA_shape (s : (DM 2 0 : Type)) :
    mpcWordLetA s = dmA 2 0 * ((dmB 2 0 ^ 4)⁻¹ * s) := by
  rw [mpcWordLetA, mul_assoc]

theorem mpcBld_letA_corr_mem {s : (DM 2 0 : Type)}
    (hs : s ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2) :
    (dmB 2 0 ^ 4)⁻¹ * s ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 := by
  refine Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.inv_mem _ ?_) hs
  have h : dmB 2 0 ^ 4 = (dmB 2 0 ^ 2) ^ 2 := by rw [← pow_mul]
  rw [h]
  exact twoCentralSeries_antitone (G := (DM 2 0 : Type)) (by omega : 2 ≤ 3)
    (sq_mem_twoCentralSeries_succ _ (sq_mem_twoCentralSeries_succ _ (Subgroup.mem_top _)))

/-- The `C̄₀`-letter is the marked `C̄₀` times a `λ₂`-element. -/
theorem mpcBld_letC_shape (m : (DM 2 0 : Type)) :
    mpcWordLetC m = dmC 2 0 * (dmB 2 0 ^ 2 * commP (dmB 2 0 ^ 2) (dmC 2 0) * m) := by
  rw [mpcWordLetC, commP]; group

theorem mpcBld_letC_corr_mem {m : (DM 2 0 : Type)}
    (hm : m ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2) :
    dmB 2 0 ^ 2 * commP (dmB 2 0 ^ 2) (dmC 2 0) * m ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 := by
  have hB2 : dmB 2 0 ^ 2 ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 :=
    sq_mem_twoCentralSeries_succ _ (Subgroup.mem_top _)
  exact Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.mul_mem _ hB2
    (twoCentralSeries_antitone (G := (DM 2 0 : Type)) (by omega : 2 ≤ 3)
      (cfour_commP_mem_three hB2 (dmC 2 0)))) hm

/-- ⭐⭐ **THE `B̄`-SLOT INCREMENT ON `D_M 2 0`.**  Multiplying the `B̄`-correction by `u ∈ λ_j`
multiplies the core word by `⁅Ā, u⁆`, exactly, modulo `λ_{j+2}`. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_t {j : ℕ} (s t m n u : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hs : s ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2)
    (hu : u ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j) :
    levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB (t * u)) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n))
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n) *
          commP (dmA 2 0) u) := by
  have hB : mpcWordLetB (t * u) = mpcWordLetB t * u := by
    rw [mpcWordLetB, mpcWordLetB, mul_assoc]
  have hA : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) (mpcWordLetA s)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) (dmA 2 0) *
        levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) ((dmB 2 0 ^ 4)⁻¹ * s) := by
    rw [mpcBld_letA_shape, map_mul]
  rw [hB, map_mul, map_mWord, map_mWord, map_mul, mpcBld_map_commP,
    mpcBld_incr_far hA ⟨_, mpcBld_letA_corr_mem hs, rfl⟩ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩]

/-- ⭐⭐ **THE `D̄`-SLOT INCREMENT ON `D_M 2 0`.**  Multiplying the `D̄`-correction by `u ∈ λ_j`
multiplies the core word by `⁅C̄₀, u⁆`, exactly, modulo `λ_{j+2}`. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_n {j : ℕ} (s t m n u : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hm : m ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2)
    (hu : u ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j) :
    levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD (n * u)))
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n) *
          commP (dmC 2 0) u) := by
  have hD : mpcWordLetD (n * u) = mpcWordLetD n * u := by
    rw [mpcWordLetD, mpcWordLetD, mul_assoc]
  have hC : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) (mpcWordLetC m)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) (dmC 2 0) *
        levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
          (dmB 2 0 ^ 2 * commP (dmB 2 0 ^ 2) (dmC 2 0) * m) := by
    rw [mpcBld_letC_shape, map_mul]
  rw [hD, map_mul, map_mWord, map_mWord, map_mul, mpcBld_map_commP,
    mpcBld_incr_near hC ⟨_, mpcBld_letC_corr_mem hm, rfl⟩ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩]

/-- ⭐⭐ **THE `Ā`-SLOT INCREMENT ON `D_M 2 0`.**  Multiplying the `Ā`-correction by `u ∈ λ_j`
multiplies the core word by `u²·⁅u, Ā⁆·⁅u, B̄-letter⁆`, exactly, modulo `λ_{j+2}`. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_s {j : ℕ} (s t m n u : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hs : s ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2)
    (hu : u ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j) :
    levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA (s * u)) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n))
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n) *
          (u ^ 2 * commP u (dmA 2 0) * commP u (mpcWordLetB t))) := by
  have hAu : mpcWordLetA (s * u) = mpcWordLetA s * u := by
    rw [mpcWordLetA, mpcWordLetA]; group
  have hA : levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) (mpcWordLetA s)
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) (dmA 2 0) *
        levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2) ((dmB 2 0 ^ 4)⁻¹ * s) := by
    rw [mpcBld_letA_shape, map_mul]
  rw [hAu, map_mul, map_mWord, map_mWord, map_mul, map_mul, map_mul, map_pow,
    mpcBld_map_commP, mpcBld_map_commP,
    mpcBld_incr_head hA ⟨_, mpcBld_letA_corr_mem hs, rfl⟩ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩]

/-- ⭐⭐ **THE PIVOT-SLOT INCREMENT ON `D_M 2 0`.**  Multiplying the `C̄₀`-correction by `u ∈ λ_j`
multiplies the core word by `⁅u, D̄-letter⁆`, exactly, modulo `λ_{j+2}`; the row-shifted fourth
power does not see it. -/
theorem mpcBld_incr_m {j : ℕ} (s t m n u : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hu : u ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j) :
    levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC (m * u)) (mpcWordLetD n))
      = levelMk (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)
        (mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA s) (mpcWordLetB t) (mpcWordLetC m) (mpcWordLetD n) *
          commP u (mpcWordLetD n)) := by
  have hCu : mpcWordLetC (m * u) = mpcWordLetC m * u := by
    rw [mpcWordLetC, mpcWordLetC]; group
  rw [hCu, map_mul, map_mWord, map_mWord, map_mul, mpcBld_map_commP,
    mpcBld_incr_pivot ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩]

/-- **The reachable increment of one rung**, from all four slots at once: the `Ā`-slot's
`u²·⁅u,Ā⁆·⁅u,b⁆`, the pivot slot's `⁅u,d⁆`, the `B̄`-slot's `⁅Ā,u⁆` and the `D̄`-slot's
`⁅C̄₀,u⁆`.  Modulo `λ_{j+2}` these commute and square to `1`, so the set of values is an
`𝔽₂`-subspace of `λ_{j+1}/λ_{j+2}`. -/
def mpcBldIncr (t n us ut um un : (DM 2 0 : Type)) : (DM 2 0 : Type) :=
  us ^ 2 * commP us (dmA 2 0) * commP us (mpcWordLetB t) * commP um (mpcWordLetD n) *
    commP (dmA 2 0) ut * commP (dmC 2 0) un

/-- ⭐⭐⭐ **ONE RUNG, WITH EVERY SLOT.**  A class-`(j+1)` solution whose defect is killed by a
reachable increment gives a class-`(j+2)` solution, explicitly.

[W86-HOUSE, as of `f0de6ad5`, amended at `0a479c6e`: the engine is SUFFICIENT, and this is the
site a builder reaches first, so the caveat belongs here too.  As of this module's own wave it
is stated once, at `mpcBld_shift_of_full_supply`: a class-`(j+2)` solution need not be a
`λ_j`-move away from a class-`(j+1)` one, so failing the supply at ONE quadruple does not show
the rung unreachable.  `mpcBldIncr`'s "the whole effect of a `λ_j`-move" is completeness over
MOVES, a different statement, and is what is proved here.

The completeness half landed one wave later, in `Instances/MpcLadder.lean`:
`mpcLad_nonempty_iff` makes the rung an IFF (a class-`(j+2)` solution exists exactly when SOME
class-`(j+1)` solution has one-step supply, the forward direction being the identity move), so
a failure proved over the WHOLE class-`(j+1)` solution set does empty the rung
(`mpcLad_eq_empty_of_no_supply`).  Read the caveat as scoped to a single quadruple from that
tree onward.  What is still NOT available at either wave is a refutation of `MpcPivShift 2`
from an empty rung; see `mpcBld_shift_of_bracket_supply`'s block.] -/
theorem mpcBld_step {j : ℕ}
    {p : (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type) × (DM 2 0 : Type)}
    (hp : p ∈ mpcWordSet (j + 1)) (us ut um un : (DM 2 0 : Type))
    (hus : us ∈ mpcWordCorr) (husj : us ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j)
    (hut : ut ∈ mpcWordCorr) (hutj : ut ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j)
    (hum : um ∈ mpcWordCorrC) (humj : um ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j)
    (hun : un ∈ mpcWordCorr) (hunj : un ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j)
    (hkill : mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA p.1) (mpcWordLetB p.2.1) (mpcWordLetC p.2.2.1)
          (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) * mpcBldIncr p.2.1 p.2.2.2 us ut um un
        ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)) :
    (p.1 * us, p.2.1 * ut, p.2.2.1 * um, p.2.2.2 * un) ∈ mpcWordSet (j + 2) := by
  obtain ⟨hp1, hp2, hp3, hp4, -⟩ := hp
  refine ⟨Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp1 hus, Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp2 hut,
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp3 hum, Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp4 hun, ?_⟩
  have hsu : p.1 * us ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 :=
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp1.1 hus.1
  have hmu : p.2.2.1 * um ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) 2 :=
    Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp3.1.1 hum.1.1
  have hassoc : mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA p.1) (mpcWordLetB p.2.1) (mpcWordLetC p.2.2.1)
        (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) * mpcBldIncr p.2.1 p.2.2.2 us ut um un
      = mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA p.1) (mpcWordLetB p.2.1) (mpcWordLetC p.2.2.1)
          (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) *
        (us ^ 2 * commP us (dmA 2 0) * commP us (mpcWordLetB p.2.1)) *
        commP um (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) * commP (dmA 2 0) ut * commP (dmC 2 0) un := by
    simp only [mpcBldIncr]; group
  rw [mpcWord_mem_iff_levelMk,
    mpcBld_incr_n (p.1 * us) (p.2.1 * ut) (p.2.2.1 * um) p.2.2.2 un hmu hunj, map_mul,
    mpcBld_incr_t (p.1 * us) p.2.1 (p.2.2.1 * um) p.2.2.2 ut hsu hutj, map_mul,
    mpcBld_incr_m (p.1 * us) p.2.1 p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2 um humj, map_mul,
    mpcBld_incr_s p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2 us hp1.1 husj, map_mul,
    ← map_mul, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, ← hassoc]
  exact (mpcWord_mem_iff_levelMk _ _).mp hkill

/-- ⭐⭐⭐ **THE RESIDUE, AS A BRACKET-SUPPLY QUESTION.**  If at every class the defect of a
class-`(j+1)` solution can be cleared by one `Ā`-bracket and one `C̄₀`-bracket of χ-trivial
`λ_j`-elements, then `MpcPivShift 2` holds - and with it the tied `√−10` datum with no clause.

This is the ladder with the guesswork removed: the increments are exact, the target layer is an
`𝔽₂`-vector space, and the hypothesis is a linear-algebra question in a finite 2-group at each
class.  Read contrapositively with wave 84's `mpcWord_shift_of_forall_class`, a *proven empty*
solution set at one class would refute `M6`; a stall of a greedy walk still proves nothing.

⚠⚠ **[W86-HOUSE, as of `f0de6ad5`: two corrections to this docstring, both against the
statement below it.**

(1) **The refutation sentence runs the wrong way, and "contrapositively" is where it goes
wrong.**  `mpcWord_shift_of_forall_class` is `(∀ k, (mpcWordSet k).Nonempty) → MpcPivShift 2`.
Its contrapositive is `¬ MpcPivShift 2 → ∃ k, mpcWordSet k = ∅`, which is the direction wave 84
states and this sentence needs the CONVERSE of.  Getting from an empty rung to a refutation
needs `MpcPivShift 2 → ∀ k, (mpcWordSet k).Nonempty`, i.e. that the ansatz is EXHAUSTIVE among
the markings, and the tree does not have that: `MpcOrbit.mpcOrb_shift_iff_marking` characterises
`MpcPivShift 2` by an arbitrary four-letter marking `(a, b, c, d)` with the four χ-values,
whereas `mpcWordSet` fixes the shape `(Ā·B̄⁻⁴·s, B̄·t, B̄²·C̄₀·m, D̄·n)` with corrections in
`mpcWordFrat ⊓ ker χ_M`.  Nothing forces a marking into that shape.  The sentence IS sound on
the other reading of "M6", the ansatz itself: a solution of the identity lies in every
`mpcWordSet k`, so an empty rung refutes the ANSATZ.  Read it that way and no further; the same
substitution is needed at `mpcBld_shift_of_full_supply`'s closing sentence, which says "the
refutation route remains wave 84's, a proven empty `mpcWordSet k`", and, as of `0a479c6e`, at
`Instances/MpcLadder.lean`'s `mpcLad_eq_empty_of_no_supply`, whose headline is "THE REFUTATION
ROUTE, NOW REACHABLE BY THE ENGINE".  That theorem is exactly right (it concludes
`mpcWordSet (j+2) = ∅`) and its headline inherits this reading; the ladder still has no
`MpcPivShift 2 → _` in either direction, its only shift-producer being
`mpcLad_shift_of_exists_supply`.

(2) **The hypothesis below is stronger than this docstring advertises**, in the direction that
misleads a builder.  "the defect of a class-`(j+1)` solution can be cleared" describes
`mpcBld_shift_of_full_supply`'s `H`, which quantifies over `p ∈ mpcWordSet (j+1)`.  This `H`
quantifies over EVERY `g ∈ λ_{j+1}`, so it asks for the two-bracket map to hit the whole layer,
not just the defects that arise.  The proof consumes it only at the defect (`H j _ _ hp5`), so
the gap is in the statement, not the argument.  A builder who can clear defects but not the
whole layer should use `mpcBld_shift_of_full_supply`, which is the honest per-solution form and
says so at its own site.]** -/
theorem mpcBld_shift_of_bracket_supply
    (H : ∀ j, 3 ≤ j → ∀ g ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 1),
      ∃ u v, u ∈ mpcWordCorr ∧ u ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j ∧
        v ∈ mpcWordCorr ∧ v ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j ∧
        g * commP (dmA 2 0) u * commP (dmC 2 0) v
          ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)) :
    MpcPivShift 2 := by
  refine mpcWord_shift_of_forall_class_four fun k hk => ?_
  induction k, hk using Nat.le_induction with
  | base => exact mpcBld_nonempty_four
  | succ k hk ih =>
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ : ∃ j, k = j + 1 := ⟨k - 1, by omega⟩
    obtain ⟨p, hp1, hp2, hp3, hp4, hp5⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨u, v, hu, huj, hv, hvj, hkill⟩ := H j (by omega) _ hp5
    refine ⟨(p.1, p.2.1 * u, p.2.2.1, p.2.2.2 * v), hp1, Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp2 hu, hp3,
      Subgroup.mul_mem _ hp4 hv, ?_⟩
    rw [mpcWord_mem_iff_levelMk,
      mpcBld_incr_n p.1 (p.2.1 * u) p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2 v hp3.1.1 hvj,
      map_mul, mpcBld_incr_t p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2.1 p.2.2.2 u hp1.1 huj, ← map_mul]
    exact (mpcWord_mem_iff_levelMk _ _).mp hkill

/-- ⭐⭐⭐ **THE RESIDUE, COMPLETE FOR THIS SHAPE.**  `mpcBld_shift_of_bracket_supply` with the
two remaining slots added.  `mpcBldIncr` is the *whole* effect of a `λ_j`-move on the four
corrections, so this hypothesis is the weakest one-step supply the ansatz admits: a
class-by-class walk that fails it has exhausted every increment of that depth, and only then is
a stall about the ansatz rather than about the walk.

One caution, load bearing.  The hypothesis quantifies over a class-`(j+1)` *solution*, and a
class-`(j+2)` solution need not be a `λ_j`-move away from one, so failing it does **not** refute
`M6`; the refutation route remains wave 84's, a proven empty `mpcWordSet k`.

⚠ [W86-LADDER5, as of `0a479c6e`: **the caution's premise is FALSE as written.**  `mpcWordSet`
is antitone, so a class-`(j+2)` solution IS a class-`(j+1)` solution and is the identity
`λ_j`-move from itself (`mpcLad_incr_one`); `mpcLad_nonempty_iff` makes the rung an iff with no
hypothesis, and `mpcLad_eq_empty_of_no_supply` gives an emptiness route this paragraph lacked:
a supply failure proved over the WHOLE class-`(j+1)` solution set empties `mpcWordSet (j+2)`,
refuting the ANSATZ (not `MpcPivShift 2` itself; the next block scopes that).  The true content
the caution protected survives in the correct form: failure at ONE chosen `p` is no evidence.
See `MpcLadder.lean`.]

[W86-HOUSE, as of `f0de6ad5`: the caution is right and the clause after the semicolon is not.
An empty `mpcWordSet k` refutes the ANSATZ, not `MpcPivShift 2`: that step needs the ansatz to
be exhaustive among the markings `mpcOrb_shift_iff_marking` quantifies over, and no such result
exists.  Full argument at `mpcBld_shift_of_bracket_supply`'s W86-HOUSE block.  So the tree
currently has NO route to refuting `MpcPivShift 2` through this ladder, only a route to
refuting this ansatz, and the two are not known to be the same question.] -/
theorem mpcBld_shift_of_full_supply
    (H : ∀ j, 3 ≤ j → ∀ p ∈ mpcWordSet (j + 1), ∃ us ut um un,
      us ∈ mpcWordCorr ∧ us ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j ∧
      ut ∈ mpcWordCorr ∧ ut ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j ∧
      um ∈ mpcWordCorrC ∧ um ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j ∧
      un ∈ mpcWordCorr ∧ un ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) j ∧
      mWord 2 (mpcWordLetA p.1) (mpcWordLetB p.2.1) (mpcWordLetC p.2.2.1)
          (mpcWordLetD p.2.2.2) * mpcBldIncr p.2.1 p.2.2.2 us ut um un
        ∈ twoCentralSeries (DM 2 0 : Type) (j + 2)) :
    MpcPivShift 2 := by
  refine mpcWord_shift_of_forall_class_four fun k hk => ?_
  induction k, hk using Nat.le_induction with
  | base => exact mpcBld_nonempty_four
  | succ k hk ih =>
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ : ∃ j, k = j + 1 := ⟨k - 1, by omega⟩
    obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨us, ut, um, un, hus, husj, hut, hutj, hum, humj, hun, hunj, hkill⟩ :=
      H j (by omega) p hp
    exact ⟨_, mpcBld_step hp us ut um un hus husj hut hutj hum humj hun hunj hkill⟩

end Increment

